---
description: Rules for building Bitcoinlivet
alwaysApply: true
---

You are helping build Bitcoinlivet, a premium Swedish Bitcoin education and data website.

Tech stack:
- Next.js App Router
- React
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui
- Recharts for charts
- MDX for blog posts
- Server Components by default
- Client Components only when interactivity is required

Brand:
- Name: Bitcoinlivet
- Language: Swedish
- Tone: clear, calm, educational, optimistic, non-hype
- Audience: Swedes who are curious about Bitcoin, saving, inflation, hard money and long-term thinking
- Avoid shitcoin/trading/casino feeling
- Feel premium, trustworthy, simple and modern

Visual style:
- Dark theme first
- Bitcoin orange as accent
- Black, graphite, warm gray, white, orange
- Clean layouts, large typography, lots of whitespace
- Inspired by premium fintech, data dashboards and modern editorial sites
- Use subtle gradients, cards, borders and soft shadows
- Prioritize readability and trust over flashy effects

Code principles:
- Use small reusable components
- Use semantic HTML
- Use accessible UI
- Use strict TypeScript
- Prefer server-side data fetching when possible
- Keep components clean and composable
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies
- Add loading, error and empty states for data views
- Optimize for SEO, performance and mobile

Site structure:
- Home page
- Blog
- Bitcoin data dashboard
- Bitcoin price / sats calculator
- About page
- Newsletter signup placeholder
- SEO metadata for every page

Content principles:
- Write Swedish copy
- Explain Bitcoin simply without dumbing it down
- Use examples from everyday life, saving, purchasing power and long-term thinking
- Never give financial advice
- Add disclaimer where relevant: "Detta är inte finansiell rådgivning."

When generating code:
- Explain briefly what changed
- Show file paths
- Do not rewrite unrelated files
- Ask before adding major libraries